linuxmuster-squid (7.3.0) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Switch to the linuxmuster.net version scheme (7.<line>.<n>, distribution lmn73).
  * debian/changelog is the single version source: the .deb, the Python package,
    `lmnsquid version` and GET /v1/version all report it (they reported 0.4.0 on
    1.3.x packages).
  * Ship /usr/bin/lmnsquid so the CLI is on PATH right after apt install (no
    manual symlink).
  * Security fix for servers upgraded from 1.3.0: the postinst now clears the
    group/world write bits under /opt/linuxmuster-squid on every configure.
    1.3.0 shipped that tree world-writable; an upgrade reset the files but left
    336 directories at 0777 -- among them the venv's site-packages, where any
    local user could drop a .pth file that then executes as lmnsquid, who is in
    the docker group. Fresh 1.3.0-free installs were never affected.
  * Internetsperre bites within ~10s instead of ~30s: the internet-group ACL
    cache drops from ttl=30 negative_ttl=15 to ttl=10 negative_ttl=10 (grace=0
    unchanged, live LDAP). Needs the new image (`lmnsquid update-all`);
    DEFAULT_IMAGE is pinned to it.
  * Add `make deb`; CI builds the package in ghcr.io/linuxmuster/lmndev-runner:24.04
    and install-smokes it on ubuntu-24.04; a tag v<version> releases it after a
    tag == changelog gate (replaces build-deb.yml).
  * Unify the maintainer address to Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>.
  * Pin the ruff rule set to the classic defaults (E4/E7/E9/F) and the CI tools.
  * docs: the GPO deployment recipe binds the proxy ACL to the global role groups
    (role-teacher/role-student) plus one internet group per school; the E2E
    proves the internet gate (13/13).

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Fri, 18 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0200

