linuxmuster-squid (1.0.0) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Project language switched to English (docs, comments, scripts).
  * Remove ROADMAP.md and the /advance-roadmap dev skill (all phases complete).
  * REUSE 3.3 compliance: SPDX headers on every file, reuse lint as a CI gate.
  * --image is optional on create (defaults to the digest-pinned DEFAULT_IMAGE);
    `lmnsquid update <name>` without an image updates to that default.
  * --school-subnets is repeatable; the API accepts comma-/space-separated lists.
  * Add `lmnsquid update-all` (POST /v1/update-all) with per-instance health
    auto-rollback; a .deb upgrade runs it automatically (best effort).
  * Update auto-rollback also covers a failing apply() (e.g. an unpullable
    image); update-all no longer aborts the batch on one bad instance.
  * _pull handles @sha256: digests; the CLI no longer times out on health-gated
    update/update-all.
  * postinst starts the service on reinstall over config-files, not only on a
    fresh install.
  * Blocking API endpoints run synchronously so a long update-all no longer
    stalls /v1/health.
  * cache.log rotation runs even with access_log_enabled: false.
  * CI shellcheck pinned to --severity=warning; fixed a real SC2164.
  * docs: healthcheck description (407 probe) and http_access order corrected.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Wed, 08 Jul 2026 07:40:36 +0200

linuxmuster-squid (1.0.0~rc3) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * .deb upgrade restarts the service (postinst try-restart; prerm stops only on
    remove) so new code is actually loaded; deb_smoke checks the MainPID change.
  * Add POST /v1/reconcile + `lmnsquid reconcile`; restore/DR runbook;
    instances_dir as a git repo (change log).
  * dockerd down -> 503 instead of a raw 500; alerting/auth-health docs.
  * Blocklist fail-closed (sanity floor) against tampered/truncated downloads.
  * Warn on a non-loopback bind (token in cleartext); add RELEASE.md.
  * docs: ECH/QUIC/DoH as a known SNI-filter limit (threat model T14); TLS
    loopback only; socket proxy pinned to :v0.4.2.

 -- Kevin Stenzel <mail@kevin-stenzel.de>  Fri, 03 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0200

linuxmuster-squid (1.0.0~rc2) lmn73; urgency=medium

  * Log retention and query: access log mirrored to docker logs, gzip-rotated
    history in the persistent log volume (log_retention_days, default 30).
  * GET /logs?since=&until=&grep= (live) and GET /logs/access (historical);
    CLI `logs` / `access-logs`.
  * access_log_enabled per instance; retention documented as the deletion
    deadline (threat model T13).

